lly will this be a bipartisan  effort  I think the president has made an effort  to make it a bipartisan issue i think  when we get down to the nuts and bolts  of it there will be those of us who will  say that the real cost savings are when  you begin to stand up to the  pharmaceutical industry well the  Republicans and some conservative  democrats support that I don't know when  you begin to demand that some physicians  do not make hundreds and hundreds of  thousands of dollars a year in salary  will the AMA and some of the people in  Congress support that I don't know and  most importantly unfortunately the  president's proposal still gives an  enormous amount of responsibility and  power to the largest insurance companies  in America I myself personally don't  believe that you're going to have a cost  effective system which is going to be  run as the president's plan proposes by  very very large insurance companies  there's going to be a lot of contention  over those issues congressman Bernie  Sanders thank you very much cheaper
 

